\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Jesus, in whom the weary find
\par Their late, but permanent repose,
\par Physician of the sin-sick mind,
\par Relieve my wants, assuage my woes;
\par And let my soul on Thee be cast,
\par Till life's fierce tyranny be past.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Loosed from my God, and far removed,
\par Long have I wandered to and fro,
\par O'er earth in endless circles roved,
\par Nor found whereon to rest below:
\par Back to my God at last I fly,
\par For O the waters still are high.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Selfish pursuits, and nature's maze,
\par The things of earth, for Thee I leave;
\par Put forth Thy hand, Thy hand of grace,
\par Into the ark of love receive,
\par Take this poor fluttering soul to rest,
\par And lodge it, Saviour, in Thy breast.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Fill with inviolable peace,
\par Stablish and keep my settled heart;
\par In Thee may all my wanderings cease;
\par From Thee no more may I depart;
\par Thy utmost goodness called to prove,
\par Loved with an everlasting love.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

